# Structured file-effect audit checklist

- [ ] Inventory uses lstat/no-follow and hashes only regular files.
- [ ] Root and descendant symlinks are detected rather than followed.
- [ ] Residual created, modified, deleted and type-changed paths are reconciled.
- [ ] Structured provider events, not command-string slash matching, classify paths.
- [ ] Create-then-delete and other transient actions remain visible through events.
- [ ] Outside-workspace, approved-output and unknown path scopes fail for model writes.
- [ ] COMPLETE observability requires every residual change to have an event.
- [ ] PARTIAL or UNKNOWN event observability can never yield PASS.
- [ ] Only exact, canonical relative paths can be authorized by policy.
- [ ] The module performs no filesystem mutation, model, Solver, DB or network action.
